import{_ as o,o as t,c as n,a2 as i}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 280 | Tang-Luo Decomposition | Absence of Law-Anchored Authority: Strong Ones Above the Law","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 280 | Tang-Luo Decomposition | Absence of Law-Anchored Authority: Strong Ones Above the Law","no":280,"module":2,"tags":["Tang-Luo","Law-Anchored Authority","Above-the-Law","Strong-One Arbitrariness","Myriad-Realms Benchmark"],"related":["40-Symbiotic Constitution Outline","49-Governance Framework and Power Checks","90-Glossary"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0280_模块2-唐罗-法则锚定权限缺失.md","filePath":"en/0280_模块2-唐罗-法则锚定权限缺失.md"}'),s={name:"en/0280_模块2-唐罗-法则锚定权限缺失.md"};function a(r,e,l,h,d,u){return t(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[i('<h1 id="entry-280-tang-luo-decomposition-absence-of-law-anchored-authority-strong-ones-above-the-law" tabindex="-1">Entry 280 | Tang-Luo Decomposition | Absence of Law-Anchored Authority: Strong Ones Above the Law <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-280-tang-luo-decomposition-absence-of-law-anchored-authority-strong-ones-above-the-law" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 280 | Tang-Luo Decomposition | Absence of Law-Anchored Authority: Strong Ones Above the Law&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Full Decomposition of the Tang-Luo System (Entry 30)</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-who-will-manage-the-strongest-person" tabindex="-1">Introduction: Who will manage the strongest person <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-who-will-manage-the-strongest-person" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: Who will manage the strongest person&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Among the six top-level axioms, the law-first axiom requires laws first. Heng Yuan Zhou has a core term — <strong>law-anchored authority</strong>: any strong one&#39;s actions must be anchored on public law, not on his personal judgment. The Tang-Luo system&#39;s greatest blank is precisely this: Tang Luo himself is above the law. This entry takes the law-first axiom as core. Protagonist uniqueness dependency judgment: <strong>Tang Luo = high dependency / bestowal-style civilization</strong>. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s evaluation base has been upgraded to six top-level axioms.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Above-the-law energy-level waste:</p><ul><li><strong>Strong-one self-consumption</strong>: Tang Luo as the strongest, no law constrains, no law protects. Every day he faces countless requests, temptations, conspiracies, all judged by himself. This mental consumption is enormous</li><li><strong>Decisions without anchor</strong>: no law as decision anchor, Tang Luo&#39;s judgment depends on intuition, experience, mood. Decision quality fluctuates widely</li><li><strong>Subordinates without basis</strong>: Tang Luo&#39;s subordinates execute his orders, but the orders themselves have no legal basis. Subordinates do not know &quot;why this is done,&quot; only follow. Once circumstances change, subordinates cannot adapt</li></ul><p>Energy-level waste: <strong>the strongest one&#39;s energy is consumed on problems that should have been solved by law.</strong></p><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Strong-one willfulness</strong>: because Tang Luo is above the law, every decision may be willful. Willful decisions repeat, civilization&#39;s expectations become unstable</li><li><strong>Subordinates mechanized</strong>: because orders have no legal basis, subordinates only follow, do not think. Tang Luo retires, subordinates all become puppets waiting for orders</li><li><strong>Rules change with person</strong>: rules Tang Luo sets today may change tomorrow by his mood. All beings cannot form stable expectations, social trust low</li></ol><p>Regression form: civilization under Tang Luo&#39;s rule looks ordered, actually order is his personal will&#39;s projection. The projection sways with his mood.</p><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Above-the-law = lawless</strong>: strong ones above the law is essentially strong ones possessing &quot;arbitrary power.&quot; Arbitrary power&#39;s predation on weak ones is more dangerous than law-based predation</li><li><strong>Not anchoring is predation</strong>: Tang Luo&#39;s actions not anchored on public law is equivalent to every decision being &quot;free discretion.&quot; Free discretion = disguised predation</li><li><strong>No supervision is predation</strong>: no one can supervise him, because no law exists to supervise him by. Absolute freedom = absolute predation potential</li></ul><p>By the Gu Chensha / Tang Luo judgment table standard: Tang Luo = <strong>enlightened predator</strong>, his predation form is &quot;arbitrary discretion.&quot; His good will limits his abuse of power, but good will itself cannot be transmitted.</p><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Tang-Luo Above-the-Law</th><th>Anchor Symbiosis Law-Anchored</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Strong-one arbitrary discretion</td><td>Law-anchored authority benefits all beings, all actions anchored on public law</td></tr><tr><td>Decisions by intuition</td><td>Decisions have legal basis, reviewable, traceable</td></tr><tr><td>Subordinates only follow</td><td>Subordinates know why, can adapt</td></tr><tr><td>Rules change with person</td><td>Laws stable, law revision requires legislative procedure</td></tr><tr><td>No supervision</td><td>Anchor Supervision Committee + Symbiotic Court, strong ones also judged</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Alternative&#39;s crux: replace &quot;Tang Luo&#39;s judgment&quot; with &quot;law&#39;s judgment.&quot; Strong ones are not above the law, but under the law.</p><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Modeling</strong>: replicate Tang-Luo arbitrary discretion model</li><li><strong>Variables</strong>: Group A no law anchor; Group B injects law-anchored authority</li><li><strong>Observation</strong>: decision stability, subordinate adaptability</li><li><strong>Review expectation</strong>: Group B decision stability rises tenfold, subordinate adaptability significantly enhanced</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Setting self-consistency: medium</strong>. Protagonist above-the-law is &quot;strong-one privilege&quot; in his world-view, self-consistent but fragile</li><li><strong>Retcon-ending risk: medium-high</strong>. Long-form late if it needs &quot;Tang Luo errs&quot; to create conflict, the early &quot;Tang Luo always right&quot; is torn; if it needs &quot;Tang Luo judged&quot; to create drama, the early &quot;Tang Luo above the law&quot; is torn</li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency</strong>: high</li></ul><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: the strongest one&#39;s energy consumed on problems that could have been legalized</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: arbitrary discretion = disguised predation</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo is a good arbitrary-discretionist, but arbitrary discretion itself is a bad institution</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: law-anchored authority benefits all beings, strong ones no exception</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: cross-plane governance must have portable laws, cannot rely on arbitrary discretion</li><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power is inherent in all; the easygoing retain a guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin erases predatory motivation, predatory involution loses meaning from the root</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s law-anchored authority is not to manage weak ones, but to manage strong ones. What the Tang-Luo system most lacks is not protection for weak ones, but constraint on the strongest. A civilization above the law, even if its ruler is a sage, is only temporary good governance — once the sage retires, good governance ends.</p><p>In the final analysis, Tang-Luo · absence of law-anchored authority described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./40-共生宪法总纲.html">40-Symbiotic Constitution Outline</a> · <a href="./49-治理框架与权力制衡.html">49-Governance Framework and Power Checks</a> · <a href="./90-术语词典.html">90-Glossary</a></li></ul>',29)])])}const m=o(s,[["render",a]]);export{g as __pageData,m as default};
